        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A. Any Employer who is delinquent for sixty (60) days or more in making payments of wages, fringe benefit fund contributions, or any Union dues which have been deducted from the wages of employees pursuant to a check-off authorization shall, at the request of the Union, furnish a satisfactory surety company's bond to guarantee payment of wages and contributions to said funds and Union dues which have been deducted from the wages of an employee pursuant to a check-off authorization as required by this Agreement. The bond shall be in the amount of $5,000.00 if the Employer has three (3) employees or fewer working under this Agreement; in the amount of $15,000.00 if the Employer has four (4) to ten (10) such employees; in the amount of $30,000.00 if the Employer has eleven (11) to twenty (20) such employees; in",
